@startuml CryptoWeb-13-uc13-monitor-security-alerts
title CryptoWeb - UC13 - Monitor Security Alerts

!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam activityFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 45

|Administrator|
start
:Open security alert monitoring;
|Core Alerts Service|
:Authenticate and require administrator role;
if (Authorized?) then (no)
  |Administrator|
  :View access denied;
  stop
endif
:List alerts using status/time/user filters;
if (Matching alerts exist?) then (no)
  |Administrator|
  :View no matching alerts;
  stop
endif
|Administrator|
:Inspect alert details and linked signals;
:Review session-risk/anomaly indicators;
if (Change alert status?) then (yes)
  :Choose an allowed status action;
  |Core Alerts Service|
  :Apply permitted status update;
  note right
    Status update endpoint is scoped
    to the authenticated user's alerts.
    Admin may inspect alerts globally,
    but cannot use it to patch another
    user's alert without ownership.
  end note
endif
|Administrator|
:View updated/available alert information;
stop
@enduml
